// r7c (A24): gradable (scalar) antonym pairs, stem-level. A negated
// gradable adjective in evidence ("not hot") does not license the antonym
// extreme in the claim ("cold"): scalar opposites admit a middle
// (lukewarm). Complementary pairs (alive/dead, true/false) are NOT listed
// here -- "not dead" DOES entail "alive".
fn gradable_antonym(a:[]u8,b:[]u8)i32{
    if(z_eq(a,"hot")==1 && z_eq(b,"cold")==1){return 1;}
    if(z_eq(a,"cold")==1 && z_eq(b,"hot")==1){return 1;}
